kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "test-infra"
purpose: "测试基础设施：Fake/Faux provider、rstest-bdd、临时目录 RAII、TUI E2E 隔离。"
valid_scope[2]: src/,tests/
requirements[7]{req_id,title,statement}:
  r1,"faux-provider","System MUST provide FauxProvider that returns pre-configured response steps without network calls for deterministic agent testing."
  r2,"test-harness-tools","System MUST test tools via rstest-bdd scenario/test functions with given/when/then typed-placeholder steps, one scenario per test function."
  r4,"temp-file-raii","All tests that create temporary files MUST use RAII-based cleanup (tempfile crate) and MUST NOT leave artifacts after execution."
  r5,"async-test-timeout",Async integration tests MUST wrap their body with with_test_timeout helper (default 10s) to prevent CI hangs on deadlock or mock failure.
  r6,"no-fixed-tmp-paths","Tests MUST NOT use hardcoded /tmp paths with fixed names; MUST use unique auto-generated paths to support parallel execution."
  r7,"bdd-framework","System MUST use rstest-bdd (not cucumber-rs) for BDD tests; each feature scenario MUST be bound to a test function; step definitions MUST use typed placeholders instead of regex."
  r8,"tui-e2e-isolation","TUI end-to-end tests (portable-pty and tmux based) MUST be isolated from the main test matrix: they MUST live in a workspace-level tests/tui_e2e/ directory (not packages/xylitol-tui/tests/), MUST be marked #[ignore] or gated behind a feature flag so they do not run under the default cargo test invocation, and MUST be invoked via a dedicated justfile target (test-tui-e2e). tmux-based smoke tests MUST additionally require the tmux binary to be present (skip with a clear message if absent) and set TERM=xterm-256color for the spawned session. Each tmux session MUST use a unique name (PID or timestamp based) to allow parallel execution, and MUST be killed via Drop guard even on test panic to avoid leaking sessions."
scenarios[8]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  r1,happy,FauxProvider is configured with text and tool call responses,agent loop runs with FauxProvider,all responses are returned without network calls and call_count is tracked
  r2,scenario,"rstest-bdd step definition exists","cargo test -- test_read_file",test passes using typed placeholder steps with scenario binding
  r4,"lsp-cleanup",LSP test creates a temp .rs file,test completes (success or panic),temp file is automatically deleted
  r5,"timeout-helper","async test uses with_test_timeout(10, future)",future exceeds 10s,test panics with timeout message instead of hanging indefinitely
  r6,"parallel-safe",two instances of config loader tests run in parallel,both use unique temp directories,no file collision or test interference
  r7,"compiles-with-rstest","project has rstest and rstest-bdd dev-dependencies",cargo test bdd,all scenarios pass with cargo test syntax without custom runner
  r8,"e2e-not-in-default",the default cargo test invocation runs,"tests/tui_e2e/ cases are present but #[ignore]","no portable-pty or tmux test executes during the default cargo test run (they only run via the dedicated target)"
  r8,"tmux-session-cleaned-on-panic","a tmux smoke test panics mid-execution",the Drop guard runs,"the tmux session is killed and no orphaned session named xyl_e2e_* remains (verifiable via tmux list-sessions)"
